      "revision": 1336336858,
      "text": "Rubroshorea palembanica is a species of flowering plant in the family Dipterocarpaceae. It is a tree native to Peninsular Malaysia, Borneo, and Sumatra. It is a tall tree, growing up to 45 metres high in riverine areas and freshwater swamp forest. It is threatened by habitat loss."
